# Expectation record for 06_control_flow/001_if_else_chains.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 001_if_else_chains
area               = 06_control_flow
description        = Deep if/else-if chains, nested conditions, nested-else binding, first-match-wins arm selection, and if without else, folded and runtime variants
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Every computation is on plain int with operands drawn from small literal tables,
so no signed overflow is possible: the largest magnitude anywhere is 500 and the
largest result is 111. There is no shift and no division by a value that can be
zero. The only pointer arithmetic is the arithmetic the language performs for a
subscript: every index into the static const tables is a literal or a loop
counter provably inside its bound, and no pointer value is printed, converted to
an integer or compared. The only remainder operations are v % 2, v % 3 and v % 5
on the strictly positive inputs 6, 9, 25, 7 and 30, so the divisor is never zero
and the dividend is never negative. Every object is initialised
before it is read: the static const tables have initialisers, the volatile
staging object vin is written before each read, and out[] elements are written
before being printed. No object is modified twice between sequence points; each
volatile write and each volatile read stands in its own statement. No aliasing
violation exists because no object is accessed through a pointer of a different
type. No uninitialised storage is read, no address is taken, and nothing depends
on padding bytes or on the relative addresses of unrelated objects. Evaluation
order is never relied upon: the several function calls appearing in one printf
argument list are pure and side-effect free, so their unspecified relative order
cannot change the printed values.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Nothing implementation-defined is printed. Plain char is never used as a value,
which matters because char signedness was measured to differ across the four
targets: signed on x86_64 and i686, unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64. Every
printed value has type int, which is 32 bits on all four targets, so no value
depends on the measured pointer and long width difference (4 bytes on i686,
8 bytes on the other three). No address, no pointer value, no sizeof result and
no floating-point value is printed. All 12 cells are therefore expected to
produce byte-identical stdout, and no target restriction is needed.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
const_classify=1 2 3 4 5 6 7
runtime_classify=1 2 3 4 5 6 7
const_nested=111 110 101 100 11 10 1 0
runtime_nested=111 110 101 100 11 10 1 0
const_nested_else=2 1 -1 -1
runtime_nested_else=2 1 -1 -1
const_first_match=1 2 3 4 1
runtime_first_match=1 2 3 4 1
const_no_else=4 9
runtime_no_else=4 9
END
